<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Gaochang Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">460 CE – 640 CE · capital Gaochang</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Chinese-ruled oasis kingdom in the Turpan basin that flourished on Silk Road trade and sponsored the pilgrim Xuanzang, before the Tang annexed it in 640.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaochang">Gaochang</a> grew from a Han military colony in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turfan">Turpan</a> basin into the seat of a commandery under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/former-liang">Former Liang</a> and its successors. After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rouran-khaganate">Rouran Khaganate</a> destroyed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-liang">Northern Liang</a> remnant there in 460, it installed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kan-bozhou">Kan Bozhou</a> as King of Gaochang. After several short-lived dynasties, the Qu family took the throne around 500 and held it until 640.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaochang">Gaochang's</a> rulers governed a largely Chinese population with Chinese-style offices, Confucian schooling and Chinese law, while paying tribute to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rouran-khaganate">Rouran</a> and later the Turks. Documents from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astana-cemetery">Astana cemetery</a> record contracts, taxes and caravans trading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, horses and slaves. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> flourished: in 630 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qu-wentai">Qu Wentai</a> welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang">Xuanzang</a> and funded his journey to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qu-wentai">Qu Wentai</a> allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/western-turkic-khaganate">Western Turkic Khaganate</a> and blocked trade to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. In 640 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hou-junji">Hou Junji</a>, Qu Wentai died as the army approached, and his son surrendered. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaochang">Gaochang</a> became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-tang">Tang</a> prefecture of Xizhou.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 460 CE – 640 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:68.86%;width:3.58%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>460 CE – 640 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gaochang</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kan Bozhou, Qu Jia, Qu Wentai</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gaochang, Kingdom of Gaochang</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=550&amp;focus=gaochang-kingdom" aria-label="Gaochang Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6844 655 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gaochang Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7164 911L7402 767M7164 911L7771 1192M7164 911L6820 913"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7402 767h0M7771 1192h0M6820 913h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7164 911h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7164 911h0"/></svg></a><f